cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the associated paper."
title: "Loa loa high-intensity risk mapping with extreme-value theory"
abstract: >-
  Bayesian joint geostatistical and extreme-value model for predicting where
  high-intensity Loa loa microfilarial loads (>20,000 mf/mL) are appreciably common,
  to support the safety of ivermectin mass drug administration in loiasis co-endemic
  areas. Applied to south-eastern Nigeria.
authors:
  - family-names: Johnson
    given-names: Olatunji
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Loa loa
  - geostatistics
  - extreme-value theory
  - generalised Pareto distribution
  - ivermectin
  - mass drug administration
  - neglected tropical diseases
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Predicting where few people carry dangerously high Loa loa microfilarial loads:
    a Bayesian joint geostatistical and extreme-value analysis to support safe
    ivermectin mass treatment in south-eastern Nigeria
  authors:
